# Words that mark text as written by Claude.
#
# Taken from the lead component of the analysis at
# https://louisabraham.github.io/load-bearing/, which measures the
# vocabulary that separates Claude-authored writing from everything
# else. That component rose from 0.9% of the corpus to 37% over 86
# weeks; the words below are its highest-lift entries, less the ones
# that are ordinary English or necessary technical terms.
#
# A word here is not forbidden where it is literally true: a lever is a
# lever, and a byte-identical file is byte-identical. It is forbidden as
# metaphor, which is how it is nearly always reached for.

